      "title": "Intl Student Services Coordinator / Designated School Official",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nInternational Student Services Coordinator / Designated School Official (DSO) Join Thomas More University in Welcoming the World Thomas More University is seeking an  International Student Services Coordinator / Designated School Official (DSO) to serve as a trusted resource for our international students and a key partner in the University’s commitment to student success, global education, and hospitality. This position provides leadership for international student services and F-1 immigration compliance while supporting students from admission through graduation. The Coordinator serves as the University’s primary operational resource for  F-1 regulations, SEVIS, SEVP requirements, and international student advising , while also helping create a welcoming and engaging campus experience. What You’ll Do Serve as a Designated School Official (DSO) and institutional resource for F-1 immigration regulations and SEVP compliance. Maintain accurate SEVIS records, Forms I-20, Form I-17 requirements, and required federal reporting and deadlines. Advise international students on maintaining F-1 status, enrollment, employment authorization, travel, academic changes, CPT, OPT, transfers, and program extensions. Monitor international student status and provide proactive outreach when academic, compliance, or personal concerns arise. Coordinate international student orientation and programs supporting cultural adjustment, engagement, retention, and student success. Support Graduate & Global Education programs, including residency weekends and related student and faculty coordination. Collaborate with Enrollment, Academic Affairs, Student Life, Athletics, Financial Aid, the Registrar, faculty, advisors, and other campus partners. Maintain Terra Dotta and other systems supporting international student services. Monitor changes in federal regulations and communicate their impact to University leadership and campus partners. Contribute to departmental projects, strategic initiatives, international partnerships, and operational improvements. What We’re Looking For Required Bachelor’s degree. Ability to become and maintain eligibility as a Designated School Official. Excellent organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Strong attention to detail and ability to manage confidential information. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively across departments. Preferred Experience with SEVIS and F-1 immigration regulations. Experience in higher education, international education, student services, advising, enrollment, or a related field. Experience with Terra Dotta or comparable international student management systems. Experience advising international students or coordinating student programs and events. A Thomas More Saint At Thomas More University, we believe how we serve matters as much as what we accomplish. The successful candidate will demonstrate the Characteristics of a Saint through: Service — Respecting and advancing the Catholic mission and identity of Thomas More University. Stewardship — Responsibly managing student records, institutional resources, regulatory requirements, and the trust placed in this role. Humility — Approaching students and colleagues with openness, respect, a willingness to listen, and a commitment to serving others. Hospitality — Creating a welcoming environment where students from around the world feel known, supported, valued, and at home. Why This Role Matters International students bring unique perspectives, cultures, and experiences that enrich the entire Thomas More community. In this role, you will help ensure that international students have both the compliance guidance and personal support they need to thrive.. If you are organized, relationship-oriented, globally minded, and passionate about helping students succeed, we invite you to join the Thomas More University community. This position requires occasional evening and weekend work, including participation in Global Education residency weekends approximately three times per year.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=620221686_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Collection and Library Services Librarian",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nThomas More University is guided by the Characteristics of a Saint : Hospitality, Humility, Service, and Stewardship . We strive to support a welcoming community that recognizes the dignity of every person, approaches learning and relationships with openness and humility, serves others with compassion and purpose, and faithfully stewards the gifts, opportunities, and responsibilities entrusted to us. These values shape our culture, inform our decisions, and inspire our commitment to educating individuals who lead lives of purpose, integrity, and service. The Collections & Library Services Librarian serves as the operational and infrastructure backbone of the Benedictine Library, ensuring that resources are accessible, systems function effectively, and collections support the curricular and institutional needs of the University. This position provides leadership in access services, collections management, library systems, and resource workflows, while also contributing targeted liaison work and outreach connected to collections and services within a collaborative, small-library environment. Principle Duties & Responsibilities:    1. Access Services & Resource Delivery Manage interlibrary loan (ILL) services Coordinate circulation, reserves, and resource delivery workflows Develop and maintain policies and procedures for access and service delivery Ensure consistent, reliable access to library resources   2. Collections & Resource Management Implement collection development decisions in collaboration with library director, R&I librarian, and faculty Manage acquisitions, subscriptions, and vendor relationships Lead collection maintenance initiatives, including weeding and evaluation Support alignment of collections with curriculum and institutional priorities   3. Cataloging, Processing & Discoverability Ensure timely processing and availability of library materials Perform or oversee copy cataloging and metadata maintenance Maintain organization and discoverability of physical and electronic resources   4. Library Systems & Technology Administer and maintain the integrated library system (e.g., Koha) Troubleshoot access and resource issues Maintain the functional and service aspects of the library website, utilizing the LibGuides Content Management System (CMS) platform   5. Government Documents (this is an electronic collection) Manage the government documents collection Ensure organization, accessibility, and compliance with applicable standards   6. Records Management & Archives Support Coordinate records intake, organization, and storage Maintain selected archival materials at a basic operational level Support institutional records retention and preservation practices   7. Outreach & Liaison (Targeted) Serve as liaison to assigned programs or departments (limited scope) Conduct outreach that promotes collections and services Support student engagement with library resources   8. Assessment & Continuous Improvement (Shared) Contribute to assessment of library services and collections Collect and analyze data to inform decision-making Support institutional reporting and accreditation processes   Additional Responsibilities Participate in campus committees and collaborative initiatives Engage in professional development and remain current with library trends and practices Perform other duties as assigned based on library priorities Education, Specialized and/or Technical Knowledge Requirements:    Master of Library Science (MLS) from an ALA-accredited program preferred Experience in academic libraries or related settings preferred Familiarity with library systems, collections, or access services desirable   Interested candidates please upload a resume and cover letter when completing the electronic application.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=620074517_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Head Coach Volleyball",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nThomas More University is guided by the Characteristics of a Saint : Hospitality, Humility, Service, and Stewardship . We strive to support a welcoming community that recognizes the dignity of every person, approaches learning and relationships with openness and humility, serves others with compassion and purpose, and faithfully stewards the gifts, opportunities, and responsibilities entrusted to us. These values shape our culture, inform our decisions, and inspire our commitment to educating individuals who lead lives of purpose, integrity, and service. Basic Purpose The Volleyball Coach for the Volleyball Program is responsible for management of all facets of the volleyball program including, but not limited to coaching/teaching, recruiting, budget management, administration,  scheduling of competitions, team travel, weekly practice sessions, hiring and supervision of assistant coaches/interns, community service, student development, and compliance with NCAA, Great Midwest conference and university rules and regulations. Principle Duties & Activities • Develop a program of athlete recruitment commensurate with the aims and goals of Thomas More  University and appropriate for a member of the NCAA, Division II. • Plan and coordinate practice and game plans for intercollegiate competition. • Determine policies and procedures for team selection and athlete participation. • Make recommendations about game schedules and budget for the team. • Track the academic progress of the volleyball student-athletes and provide appropriate advice and assistance to help insure the successful completion of each players stated program of study. • Develop and implement a comprehensive fundraising program to raise funds necessary to offset expenses associated for non-budgeted expenses and spring training trips.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=605603259_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct Assistant Professor of Marketing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nAbout the Role: The Adjunct Assistant Professor of Marketing plays a pivotal role in delivering high-quality marketing education to undergraduate and/or graduate students within an academic institution. This position is responsible for designing and delivering engaging course content that reflects current marketing theories, practices, and trends, thereby preparing students for successful careers in the marketing field. The role involves fostering a dynamic and inclusive learning environment that encourages critical thinking, creativity, and practical application of marketing concepts. Additionally, the professor will contribute to curriculum development and collaborate with faculty members to enhance the overall academic program. Ultimately, this position aims to inspire and equip students with the knowledge and skills necessary to excel in the evolving marketing landscape while supporting the institution’s mission of academic excellence and student success. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Marketing, Business Administration, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Demonstrated expertise in marketing principles and practices through academic or professional experience. Prior teaching experience at the college or university level is preferred but not mandatory. Strong communication and interpersonal skills to effectively engage with diverse student populations. Eligibility to work in the United States. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree (Ph.D. or DBA) in Marketing or a related discipline. Experience with online or hybrid course delivery platforms and instructional technologies. Professional marketing experience in industry sectors such as digital marketing, brand management, or market research. Record of scholarly activity or contributions to marketing research and publications. Experience mentoring students and supporting their professional development. Responsibilities: Develop and deliver course materials for marketing classes, including lectures, assignments, and assessments. Engage students through interactive teaching methods and provide timely feedback to support their academic growth. Stay current with marketing industry trends and integrate relevant real-world examples into the curriculum. Participate in departmental meetings and contribute to curriculum review and development processes. Maintain regular office hours to advise and mentor students on academic and career-related matters. Skills: The required and preferred skills are utilized daily to create an effective and engaging learning environment. Strong communication skills enable clear explanation of complex marketing concepts and foster meaningful interactions with students. Expertise in marketing theory and practice allows the professor to design relevant coursework that bridges academic knowledge with real-world application. Familiarity with instructional technologies supports the delivery of content in various formats, including in-person and online settings. Additionally, interpersonal and mentoring skills are essential for guiding students’ academic progress and career aspirations, ensuring they receive comprehensive support throughout their educational journey.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=663218564_3&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Senior Vice President and Chief Financial Off",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nThomas More University is a Catholic university dedicated to educating students to lead lives of purpose, integrity, faith, and service. Guided by its core values of Hospitality, Humility, Service, and Stewardship, the University seeks a strategic and collaborative financial leader to advance its mission while ensuring long-term financial vitality and institutional sustainability. Position Overview The Senior Vice President & Chief Financial Officer serves as the University's chief financial officer and principal financial advisor to the President, Senior Leadership Team, and Board of Trustees. Reporting directly to the President, the CFO provides strategic leadership for the University's financial resources and operations while helping position the institution for sustained growth and success. The CFO oversees: Financial planning and analysis Budgeting and forecasting Accounting and financial reporting Treasury and cash management Endowment and investment oversight Debt management Audit and regulatory compliance Risk management Capital planning and financial sustainability initiatives The CFO also works closely with enrollment leadership to support tuition revenue strategy, financial aid planning, and student success initiatives in a competitive higher education environment. Key Leadership Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Serve as a strategic advisor to the President and Board of Trustees Lead long-range financial planning and institutional financial modeling Guide annual operating and capital budgeting processes Support institutional decision-making through data-driven financial analysis Strengthen relationships with financial institutions, investment advisors, and external partners Oversee financial operations and key administrative functions Promote a culture of accountability, transparency, collaboration, and responsible stewardship Lead initiatives that support Thomas More University's financial vitality and strategic growth Preferred Qualifications Candidates should possess: Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or related discipline Master's degree preferred CPA strongly preferred Seven or more years of progressive financial leadership experience Experience working in higher education, particularly at a private, tuition-dependent institution, strongly preferred Experience working with governing boards and board committees Demonstrated expertise in financial strategy, budgeting, forecasting, investments, and institutional planning The ideal candidate will be: Mission-centered Strategic and forward-thinking Collaborative and relationship-oriented Steward-minded Analytical and decisive Transparent and trustworthy Innovative and growth-focused Service-oriented in leadership style About Thomas More University Applicants should submit: Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for Three Professional References Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The University anticipates appointing its next Senior Vice President & Chief Financial Officer by February 2027",
      "department": ""
    },
