    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=648921142_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Gallery Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-05\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nAbout the Role: The Gallery Assistant plays a vital role in supporting the daily operations and educational mission of the gallery within an educational services environment. This position is responsible for facilitating visitor engagement, assisting with exhibition preparation, and ensuring the smooth functioning of gallery activities. The Gallery Assistant will collaborate closely with curators, educators, and administrative staff to enhance the visitor experience and promote the gallery's educational programs. By managing logistical tasks and providing excellent customer service, the Gallery Assistant helps maintain a welcoming and informative environment for diverse audiences. Ultimately, this role contributes to the gallery’s goal of fostering appreciation and understanding of art and culture within the community. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent. Experience in customer service or a related role involving public interaction. Basic knowledge of art or museum/gallery environments. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to lift and move objects up to 25 pounds safely. Preferred Qualifications: Associate or Bachelor’s degree in Art History, Museum Studies, Education, or a related field. Experience working in a gallery, museum, or educational setting. Familiarity with art handling and installation techniques. Proficiency with gallery management software or databases. Excellent communication skills and ability to work collaboratively in a team environment. Responsibilities: Assist in the installation and deinstallation of exhibitions, ensuring artworks and displays are handled with care and according to established protocols. Greet and provide information to visitors, answering questions about exhibitions, programs, and gallery policies in a professional and courteous manner. Support educational programming by preparing materials, coordinating with educators, and facilitating group visits or tours as needed. Maintain the cleanliness and organization of gallery spaces, including public areas, storage, and workspaces. Manage administrative tasks such as scheduling, inventory tracking, and data entry to support gallery operations and reporting. Skills: The Gallery Assistant utilizes strong interpersonal skills daily to engage with visitors and provide informative, welcoming experiences. Organizational skills are essential for managing exhibition logistics, scheduling, and maintaining orderly gallery spaces. Attention to detail ensures that artworks are handled properly and that educational materials are prepared accurately. Communication skills facilitate effective collaboration with curators, educators, and other staff members to support programming and operations. Additionally, basic technical skills, including familiarity with gallery software and data entry, help streamline administrative tasks and contribute to the overall efficiency of the gallery.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=664484054_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-05\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nThomas More University Exempt Job Description Title: Admissions Counselor Department: Undergraduate Admissions Reports to: Director of Admissions Created: April 28, 2026   Thomas More University is guided by the  Characteristics of a Saint :  Hospitality, Humility, Service, and Stewardship . We strive to support a welcoming community that recognizes the dignity of every person, approaches learning and relationships with openness and humility, serves others with compassion and purpose, and faithfully stewards the gifts, opportunities, and responsibilities entrusted to us. These values shape our culture, inform our decisions, and inspire our commitment to educating individuals who lead lives of purpose, integrity, and service. Basic Purpose This position serves as a member of the Enrollment Team in the department of Undergraduate Admissions. This position is responsible for planning and implementing recruitment and enrollment functions of high school students from specific territories, as well as assist the Assistant Director of Admissions and CRM Manager with data entry and queries in the University’s Technolutions Slate software.  What You Will Bring 1. Excellent written, oral and listening skills. 2. Strong creative, strategic, analytical, organizational, and personal skills. 3. Communication and marking skills.  4. Commitment to working with shared leadership and in cross-functional teams. 5. Must show evidence of ability to manage multiple projects at a time. 6. Demonstrates strong decision-making skills and self-assurance. 7. Ability to manage data and build queries in the CRM software What You Will Do Serves as a member of the Enrollment Team managing a recruitment territory to assist in achieving enrollment goals for the University. Implement recruitment strategies as outlined in the admissions plan in the assigned territory to include high school and/or community college visits, attends college fairs, area receptions, and events. Works with students, parents and/or alumni organizations that assist with the recruitment of students. Provides admission presentations to visitors during campus daily tours and at on campus and off[1]campus events. Advises students and families of admission requirements, transfer guidelines, financial aid and scholarship information, residence life, etc. Provides follow-up to students and parents via phone, letters, email, text, and scheduled appointments in specific recruitment territory. Review admission applications, evaluates credentials, and makes admission decisions. Completes routine reports related to recruitment, projections, personal schedule, travel, special programs, and professional development. Provide support to the Assistant Director of Admissions and CRM Manager with data entry, reports, queries, communication flows, and events within the Technolutions Slate CRM software.  Adhere to University policies and procedures regarding travel and procurement. Initiates, plans, and executes special projects in conjunction with the goals and objectives of the office. Compliance with NCAA the Great Midwest conference and university rules and regulations.   Education, Specialized and/or Technical Knowledge Requirements Bachelor’s Degree Required.  Experience in Recruitment, communications/ marketing, and Higher Education preferred.  Valid Drivers License required. Travel Moderate within a designated region",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=664005798_4&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\n\nLocation: Covington\n\nMission  Covington Latin School empowers bright young men and women to achieve their full potential through a rigorous Catholic classical education, preparing them for lives of purpose, leadership, and service. Vision  To be a premier Catholic academic institution that inspires intellectual curiosity, moral integrity, and a lifelong love of learning, grounded in faith and the pursuit of excellence. Core Values Faith: We embrace and live out our Catholic identity in word and action. Excellence: We strive for the highest academic and personal standards. Integrity: We act with honesty, respect, and responsibility. Service: We value compassion, humility, and a commitment to others. Community: We foster a supportive environment of collaboration and respect. Principal Duties & Responsibilities: The Coordinator of Front Office at Covington Latin plays a pivotal role in ensuring the smooth and efficient operation of the school’s front office environment. This position serves as the primary point of contact for students, parents, staff, and visitors, providing exceptional customer service and managing communications with professionalism and warmth. The coordinator oversees daily administrative tasks, coordinates schedules, and supports the front office team to maintain an organized and welcoming atmosphere. By managing information flow and facilitating effective communication, this role directly contributes to the positive experience of all stakeholders and supports the overall mission of Covington Latin School. The ideal candidate will be proactive, detail-oriented, and capable of multitasking in a dynamic educational setting while upholding confidentiality and school policies. Essential Responsibilities Greet and assist students, parents, faculty, and visitors in a courteous and professional manner. Manage incoming calls, emails, and correspondence, directing inquiries to appropriate personnel. Coordinate and maintain schedules for front office staff and school events, ensuring efficient use of resources. Maintain accurate records, including attendance logs, visitor sign-ins, and office supplies inventory. Support administrative tasks such as processing forms, managing databases, and preparing communications. Collaborate with other departments to facilitate smooth operations and timely information dissemination. Handle sensitive information with discretion and maintain confidentiality in all interactions. Train and supervise front office support staff and volunteers as needed. Support safety and emergency response procedures in coordination with school leadership. Core Competencies Skills Required:   Ability to manage multiple priorities efficiently while maintaining attention to detail. Strong interpersonal and communication skills in working with students, families, faculty, and visitors. Proficiency with office software and technology (Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, etc.). Demonstrated ability to handle sensitive information with discretion and maintain confidentiality. Commitment to the mission and values of a Catholic educational environment. Education and Specialized and/or Technical Knowledge Requirements:   High school diploma or equivalent required; associate degree or higher preferred. Minimum of two years’ experience in an administrative or front office role, preferably in an educational environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Outlook) and standard office equipment. Strong organizational and multitasking abilities. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications:  Experience working in a private school or academic institution. Familiarity with student information systems and database management. Ability to speak a second language is a plus. Training or certification in office administration or customer service. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in a team-oriented environment. Physical Job Requirements: Frequently sitting, standing, and walking in an office or school environment. Light lifting and carrying supplies, files, etc. Proficiency in operating standard office equipment. Ability to manage multiple tasks under time constraints. Effective communication both in person and via phone or email.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=679613513_3&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "IT Help Desk Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-10\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nUniversity Overview Thomas More provides a Catholic education that goes beyond academics, nurturing intellectual, personal, and spiritual growth. Guided by four core values known as the Characteristics of a Saint : Hospitality, Humility, Service, and Stewardship , we strive to foster a welcoming community that recognizes the dignity of every person, approaches learning and relationships with openness and humility, serves others with compassion and purpose, and faithfully stewards the gifts, opportunities, and responsibilities entrusted to us. These values shape our culture, inform our decisions, and inspire our commitment to educating individuals who lead lives of purpose, integrity, and service. Our mission, rooted in the Catholic Intellectual Tradition, is to educate with purpose—helping students reach their potential while serving the greater good. Position Summary The Help Desk Specialist works within IT Services to provide reliable and high-quality technical support to the Thomas More University and Covington Latin School communities. This includes responding effectively to technical issues and requests made to the Help Desk, providing technical support for campus events, and driving continuous improvement in service delivery. This position also trains and mentors student helpdesk specialists. Required Skills Demonstrated customer-service skills in a technology environment, including the ability to explain technical issues and solutions clearly to nontechnical users Demonstrated ability to use technical troubleshooting and active-listening skills to understand, diagnose, resolve, and document technical issues Proficiency supporting Microsoft 365, Windows operating systems, computer peripherals, and mobile devices, including diagnosing common configuration, connectivity, and usability issues Experience supporting and maintaining instructional and multi-media equipment such as Projectors, Televisions, and Audio equipment. Preferred Skills  Experience with ticketing systems and knowledge management tools Proficiency with classroom technology and AV support Ability to follow information-security, identity-verification, access-control, and data-privacy procedures when supporting users and handling institutional information Experience supporting user accounts, password resets, multifactor authentication, permissions, and basic identity and access management processes Job-Related Activities  User Support, Training, and Documentation Respond effectively to technical issues and requests made via email, phone, walk in, and through the ticketing system Coordinate user support services for desktops, laptops, peripherals, and other campus technologies Support instructional technology and equipment, including classroom systems and faculty technology needs with the exception of specialized equipment or software Develop and maintain knowledge base content, support documentation, and help desk scripts to ensure consistent, high-quality service delivery Create and publish user-facing materials to support self-service and effective technology use Support student and employee onboarding and continuous learning related to institutional technologies Coordinate and deliver end-user training in partnership with campus stakeholders Support technology needs for campus events, including setup, troubleshooting, and on-site or on-call assistance Train and mentor student workers Process Improvement & Service Excellence Identify and implement opportunities to streamline operations and enhance the user experience Apply IT service management best practices Contribute to institutional initiatives related to service quality, effectiveness, and digital transformation Serve as a liaison between IT and campus departments to ensure alignment of help desk services and expectations Collaborate with IT teams on system implementations, upgrades, and support transitions Serve on Event Logistics Team and Space Utilization Committee Other duties as assigned This position operates in a collaborative campus environment and may require occasional evening or weekend work to support critical system needs or campus initiatives Education, Specialized and/or Technical Knowledge Requirements  Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Information Systems, or related field Professional experience providing IT support or working in help desk operations. Experience developing or delivering user training materials, sessions, or programs. Physical Job Requirements Tools and Equipment Used Personal computer, copier, phone and other typical office equipment Travel Minimal – less than 5% of the time Physical & Mental Demands Ability to work at a computer terminal for extended periods of time Digital dexterity and hand/eye coordination in operation of all assigned equipment Ability to speak to and hear employees/students via phone or in person Body motor skills sufficient to enable incumbent to move around all areas of the campus Capable of lifting equipment up to 30 pounds Ability to analyze data and other reports and make recommendations Mental requirements include: compare, decide, direct, problem solve, analyze, instruct, interpret",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=679328068_11&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Data and Reporting Engineer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-10\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nUniversity Overview Thomas More provides a Catholic education that goes beyond academics, nurturing intellectual, personal, and spiritual growth. Guided by four core values known as the Characteristics of a Saint : Hospitality, Humility, Service, and Stewardship , we strive to foster a welcoming community that recognizes the dignity of every person, approaches learning and relationships with openness and humility, serves others with compassion and purpose, and faithfully stewards the gifts, opportunities, and responsibilities entrusted to us. These values shape our culture, inform our decisions, and inspire our commitment to educating individuals who lead lives of purpose, integrity, and service. Our mission, rooted in the Catholic Intellectual Tradition, is to educate with purpose—helping students reach their potential while serving the greater good. Position Summary The Data and Reporting Engineer manages data from various sources, ensuring data quality and integrity, to create meaningful reports for stakeholders. This position plays a key role in strengthening the University’s data and reporting environment enabling a culture of data literacy and data-informed decision-making. This is a highly technical and collaborative role. Required Skills Commitment to data accuracy, confidentiality, security, and responsible data use Proficiency in SQL and database management systems Programming skills for data processing and automation, preferably C# and R Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Excellent communication skills to work effectively with cross-functional teams and end-users and clearly explain technical topics to non-technical users Ability to adapt to evolving technologies and trends in data engineering and reporting Preferred Skills  Understanding of data governance and data security principles Experience presenting to a large group and leadership Familiarity with reporting and visualization tools Job-Related Activities  Data Engineering Gather and connect University data from diverse sources, such as databases, APIs, and flat files Clean, transform, and preprocess data to ensure accuracy and consistency Create and maintain database objects, queries, views, stored procedures, and other data solutions that support institutional reporting and analytics Identify opportunities to automate manual data collection, transformation, validation, and reporting processes Collaborate with IT Services and functional system owners on integrations, system changes, and data-related projects Data Quality and Governance Implement data quality checks and validation processes Identify data discrepancies and inconsistencies across systems and work with appropriate data owners to resolve them Contribute to the development and maintenance of institutional data definitions, data dictionaries, reporting standards, and documentation Monitor data processes and troubleshoot issues affecting data availability, accuracy, and reliability Audit reporting outputs to ensure accuracy, consistency, and alignment with institutional definitions Institutional Reporting and Analytics Develop, maintain, and improve recurring institutional reports and reporting processes Collaborate with end-users to define and translate reporting requirements into effective technical and analytical solutions Develop dashboards, visualizations, and self-service reporting tools that allow campus users to access and understand institutional data Support reporting related to enrollment, student success, academics, faculty and staff, finance, operations, and other institutional priorities Assist with federal, state, accreditation, regulatory, and other external reporting requirements as assigned Documentation and Knowledge Sharing Document data sources, business rules, calculations, processes, and reporting methodologies Promote responsible and appropriate use of institutional data Work collaboratively to understand data needs and develop solutions Translate technical data concepts into clear, understandable language for non-technical audiences Provide training and support related to reporting tools, dashboards, data definitions, and self-service reporting Collaborate with team members and end-users to share knowledge and best practices Technical Expertise Remain up-to-date with emerging technologies and best practices in data engineering and reporting Continuously enhance skills in SQL, data modeling, and reporting tools Education, Specialized and/or Technical Knowledge Requirements  Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Data Analytics, or related field Experience in database management, data analysis, or data visualization Physical Job Requirements Tools and Equipment Used Personal computer, copier, phone and other typical office equipment Travel Minimal – less than 5% of the time Physical & Mental Demands Ability to work at a computer terminal for extended periods of time Digital dexterity and hand/eye coordination in operation of all assigned equipment Ability to speak to and hear employees/students via phone or in person Body motor skills sufficient to enable incumbent to move around all areas of the campus Capable of lifting equipment up to 30 pounds Ability to analyze data and other reports and make recommendations Mental requirements include: compare, decide, direct, problem solve, analyze, instruct, interpret",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
